//RS     // ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//RS     // D-ALLOC2 / D-REGION1 (ratified 2026-06-21): scope-bound arena `view`s.
//RS     //
//RS     // `x :: arena.alloc(v)` makes `x` a *view* into `arena`'s storage — Rust
//RS     // `&'arena mut T`. The view is sound only while it stays inside its region
//RS     // (the lexical scope of the `arena` binding / an explicit `region`) and only
//RS     // until `arena` is reset or closed. Two diagnostics enforce that, both
//RS     // *strictly* at least as strict as Rust's borrow checker, so every
//RS     // Jet-accepted program is rustc-accepted (I2: Jet rejects first):
//RS     //   * E0631 — the view escapes its region (returned, stored in a binding /
//RS     //     ref / struct field, passed where ownership/`mut` is taken, captured by
//RS     //     an escaping closure).
//RS     //   * E0632 — the view is used after the backing arena was reset.
//RS     //
//RS     // v1 restriction (I8): views are non-reassignable, non-escaping locals; we
//RS     // reject anything the analysis can't prove with a teaching error rather than
//RS     // attempt a clever lowering.
//RS     // ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
